===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|not comparable}} [[prior|Prior]]; occurring [[before]] something else, either in [[time]] or [[order]].
#: {{ux|en|He is no better than the '''previous''' Prime Minister.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=Foreword|passage=He stood transfixed before the unaccustomed view of London at night time, a vast panorama which reminded him {{...}} of some wood engravings far off and magical, in a printshop in his childhood. They dated from the '''previous''' century and were coarsely printed on tinted paper, with tinsel outlining the design.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Nick Paton Walsh|title=Ukraine ceasefire call is aimed at forcing Putin to reveal his war goals to Trump|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/10/europe/ukraine-ceasefire-call-intl-latam|date=2025-05-10|passage=Putin’s answered by simply stating he did not believe Ukraine had honored the '''previous''' ceasefires Moscow had unilaterally called, and that Kyiv has said Moscow never respected either.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251125133447/https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/10/europe/ukraine-ceasefire-call-intl-latam|archivedate=25 November 2025}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} {{U|premature}}; acting or occurring too [[soon]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Gerald Lynch|title=Roughnecks, Drillers, and Tool Pushers|passage=I was a bit '''previous''' it turned out, as I worked short-handed for ten days before I could find another hand.}}

